# Profile Pages Structure and APIs

## Pages Overview
- Public Profile: [profiles/student/[id]/page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/profiles/student/[id]/page.tsx)
- Edit Profile: [profiles/student/edit/page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/profiles/student/edit/page.tsx)

## Key Features
- Profile image upload with hover overlay and camera icon
- Public/private profile views using 'me' as ID for personal profile
- Consistent navbar with user dropdown across pages

## Required APIs
1. `/api/user/profile`
   - GET: Fetch current user's profile
   - PUT: Update user profile
   - Required fields: name, email, role, profileImage

2. `/api/user/profile/[id]`
   - GET: Fetch specific user's profile by ID
   - Special case: ID='me' returns current user's profile
   - Required fields: same as above, plus public/private data handling

3. `/api/user/profile/image`
   - POST: Upload new profile image
   - Required: Image file validation and processing
   - Returns: URL of uploaded image

## Implementation Notes
- Profile images should be stored in cloud storage (AWS S3/Firebase)
- User authentication required for edit profile and image upload
- Public profiles should have limited data visibility
- Consistent error handling across all endpoints
